INFO 03-28 14:00:14 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-b1122ac7ce454d17ba3caf183076b1cc-0: prompt: 'can you explain the following email to a 5 year old:\n\nThank you both for coming down here and spending the time with me yesterday. I really enjoyed our conversation and am excited about the opportunity for us to work together. Thinking about things on the drive back and last night, I thought I’d put together a bit of a list of questions, requests, information, etc.\n\n \n\nThe idea here is to give you as much as I can my perspective, the gaps I have in my knowledge and allow you to correct me where necessary, fill in information or benefit from some perspectives. In these, and going forward, I’m going to give myself permission to ask anything, make any observation and be completely frank. You both then need to feel completely free to only give me information you think I need and not allow yourself to get hurt feelings. If I ask for something that is confidential, that you’d just rather not respond to now, or that might seem incorrect, unfair or off base, you don’t have to feel obligated to explain or respond.\n\n \n\nThe key to us becoming creative and successful together is building a foundation of mutual trust and respect. Clear, open and comfortable channels of communication will help us build that foundation and become the most creative, complimentary team that we can.\n\n \n\nFrom that perspective, I’ll divide my thoughts, comments and questions by operational area:\n\n \n\nToronto Tunnel Project.\n\nThis seems to be the most immediate opportunity before you.\nAs I understand it, the status is:\nThere is a CAD$30 billion private fund standing ready to fund this project.\n i. You have a Letter of Intent, or some sort of document, evidencing this fund’s interest in funding the project.\n\nThe Mayor of Toronto (John Tory, I believe) is a supporter and holds a key to an immediate next step in the approval process.\n i. I believe you indicated that the next phase of approval could happen within a few weeks and would trigger a release of $3 million to $5 million funding the next phase of initial development of the project.\n\nThe project is to build freeway or roadway tunnels under significant parts of Toronto, creating additional traffic capacity.\n i. I gather that the private fund would be the owners and probably the tunnels would be toll operations?\n\nI saw a YouTube video from a news channel about five years ago describing something like this.\nBill has spearheaded the project and because of that, your firm has control of the EPC element as the project continues.\nThe project is expected to take six to eight years once construction starts.\n i. The plasma drilling technology could knock a couple of years off the project, but will require significant electricity input (50 MW).\n\n ii. May be able to work in construction of renewable energy generation as part of the project.\n\nWhat I would like to see to help me get oriented, better understand the project and the reality of it, and begin to help you advance it:\nAny project Proposals, descriptions, write ups, white papers, etc.\nAny applications or permits which have been received, applied for, upon which work has begun or a list of those needed.\nAny agreements or intended agreements with other firms which are necessary to accomplish the project.\n i. Basic construction trades, physical works, etc.\n\n ii. Other engineering, construction management, compliance, safety, governmental affairs, legal. All professional level work that needs to be done and who will help us to do it.\n\n iii. A list of all regulatory approvals and permits required to plan, commence, execute and finish the project. Copies of any approvals or permits received, applications prepared or in process.\n\nAny information available about the CAD$30 billion private fund, name, entity description, any financials or other historical information received from that fund.\n i. A copy of the Letter of Intent and any other documentation of discussions, agreements, intentions or commitments.\n\nCopies of proposals, project descriptions, financial results and finished product related to similar projects which your firm has recently completed successfully.\n i. This will help me understand your capabilities and will help me in the future to explain to others why and how you can accomplish a project of this magnitude.\n\nAny other information, preferably from external sources, talking about the project, the private investment fund and their benefits and the reasons why Toronto residents should want to invest in this project and how it will improve life in Toronto.\nEarlier in our discussions you mentioned being shortlisted for a Puerto Rico wind farm project. I don’t know if that is still alive, but assume that the Proposal would be from your existing Canadian company. If that project is still alive, it would also help me to understand that opportunity as best I can.\n \n\nU. S. Operations.\n\nThere are three thrusts of this strategy.\nCreate a project or projects to build privately owned transmission lines.\nCreate a project or projects to acquire and store inventory for provision to the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) or local utilities for emergency storm repair.\nBegin bidding on transmission construction Requests for Proposal (RFP) and perhaps other energy or general public works projects.\nPrivately owned transmission lines.\nConcept here is to locate an investor interested in owning and operating transmission lines, locate an underserved area and create an EPC project to permit, construct and perhaps operate the transmission lines.\n i. Need to identify potential investors.\n\nScope is nationwide, but particularly critical areas include California, Texas and the Eastern Seaboard.\nCurrently we don’t know if privately owned transmission is allowed, desired or encouraged.\n i. Need to identify regulators and infrastructure owners and operators.\n\n ii. Need to identify physical areas of opportunity. Where are new transmission lines needed?\n\n iii. Need to identify process for permitting, intertying and operating private transmission lines.\n\nStorm and disaster recovery inventory.\nTurkish supplier can supply materials of appropriate quality and at favorable pricing and terms.\nNeed to identify purchasing structure for FEMA or local utilities. How do we become visible and approved as an emergency supplier.\n i. How does pricing and delivery work?\n\nNeed to identify geographic areas of need, most efficient geographic area for storage and maintenance.\nNeed to build economic model based upon statistical hurricane and ice storm frequency and areas affected, previous supplier responses, expected average dwell time for inventory and carrying costs of inventory to evaluate pricing and reality of business model.\nYou mentioned a B. C. lady who has contracts or a relationship with a broker to supply manned trucks for disaster response. She has six trucks, but only two are operational at the moment. Possible opportunity to partner with her or step into her business, provide manned service trucks as opposed to or in complement to inventory for disaster recovery.\n i. Need to flesh this opportunity out, look at economics, average idle time for crews and equipment, possible infill work to keep assets and men busy while waiting for disasters, etc.\n\nBidding on RFPs and just wading into the general construction market in the U. S.\nNeed to develop understanding of competitors in marketplace. How much room is there for a new EPC supplier? What is the pricing appetite of current suppliers, how will our appearance on the bid landscape effect pricing.\nNeed to learn each customer, utility, municipality who request these types of projects, identify their required qualifications and get ourselves qualified to bid, or partner with an entity who already is qualified.\n i. Form entity.\n\n ii. Get Contractor License.\n\n iii. Insurance?\n\n iv. Bonding?\n\n v. Sufficient heft on balance sheet to qualify for EPC type work (net equity, cash or investments, etc.).\n\n vi. Any other regulatory permits or operating permissions necessary.\n\nNeed to identify who our suppliers will be.\n i. Hard goods, probably still your Turkish supplier.\n\n ii. Poles.\n\n iii. Labor.\n\n iv. Basic trades and construction services.\n\n v. Compliance.\n\n vi. Safety.\n\n vii. Legal.\n\n viii. Other necessary infrastructure to accomplish a project from start to finish.\n\nWe can use our Caterpillar Club connections to help learn a lot of the above, and perhaps to build relationships which will help infill suppliers, strategic partners, etc.\n i. Doug Veerkamp – Placerville area in California.\n\n ii. Kevin and Jennifer Ghilotti – Petaluma and Bay Area in California.\n\n iii. Dave Wintermute – Vollers Construction and Recycling – New Jersey.\n\n iv. Jeff Huff – Huff Equipment, owns and rents construction equipment, does construction in Southern and Central New York State.\n\n v. Probably others who could also help us and benefit from a relationship with us.\n\n \n\nI truly believe you have some great ideas and I think we will make a good team working together to see those ideas bear fruit.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [4814, 498, 10339, 279, 2701, 2551, 311, 264, 220, 20, 1042, 2310, 1447, 13060, 498, 2176, 369, 5001, 1495, 1588, 323, 10164, 279, 882, 448, 752, 13671, 13, 358, 2167, 14006, 1039, 10435, 323, 1079, 12035, 911, 279, 6638, 369, 601, 311, 975, 3786, 13, 52289, 911, 2513, 389, 279, 