INFO 03-28 14:00:14 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-ac897f8d8e5c4184b4a7d9aea2a16310-0: prompt: "Create a 2000 words article conversational article and Rephrase this with 100% no plagiarism and unique \nSharjah Light Festival is the massive success of Feb 2023!\nSharjah's favorite cultural light festival is back for its 12th year!! A big annual event held in the UAE, reimagining the city into a colorful display of light and music. This year's festival started on Feb 8 and is attracting thousands of visitors across all nationalities, worldwide.\n\nCutting–edge technology, allowing for seamless integration of 3D projection of lights and sound makes this SLF bigger and better than ever. The diverse array of light installations, including interactive displays, and laser shows that light up the city's iconic buildings, parks, and public spaces, enhances the emirate's exemplary architecture.\n\nThere are 14 shows and a wide range of activations of the SLF, taking place across 13 locations in Sharjah, Al Hamriyah, Eastern and Central Regions.\n\nIntroducing the Light Village for the 1st time\n\nCherish time with family and friends with special exhibitions of light-inspired installations, enjoying different cuisines under the shining stars of Sharjah at the Light Village. The Light Village has over 40 F&B outlets, offering a vast range of tastes to suit all palates. The Light Village also includes a light museum, displaying beautiful conceptual light-inspired exhibits and play area with a variety of games.\n\nHighlights of Light Village 2023:\n\nPerfect place for the sports enthusiasts\n\nSky High – Basketball area: All players, whether regular or seasonal, are encouraged to take part and elevate their sports skills. A unique and exciting atmosphere creates a dynamic activation accommodating players across all ages with different hoop heights.\n\nDancing Laser Lights\n\nEnigma – The Laser Tunnel: Visitors tantalize with curiosity, experiencing the vibrant sound and dynamic choreography of the laser lights. The laser light tunnel draws visitors into a world of enigmatic lights and sounds.\n\nLight filled faces\n\nVisage – The Faces: An array of illuminated faces greets visitors, enhancing the user's creativity and encouraging a thought-provoking mindset. From different angles, the installation takes on different views, featuring the instagrammable light technique.\n\nLittle stars – Kids area: Kids can take part in a variety of activities, including festival skill games, arcade games, thrilling riders, etc. which gives them power-packed engagement and fun.\n\nReady to explore the Light Village? Visit now!\n\nThe Light Shows of the Sharjah Light Festival highlight the beautiful architecture and stunning attractions of the emirate\n\nAl Majaz waterfront:\n\nOne of Sharjah's iconic landmarks, a popular entertainment hub for visitors and residents. The vast area dazzles with over 150 pixels of radiant LED light, creating a remarkable 3D visual experience. Enjoy rich traditional and international cuisine, take a ride in the boat with family and friends, and enjoy the Sharjah Light Festival installation by the water.\n\nKhalid Lagoon Corniche:\n\nEnjoy the Art Walk from Al Noor Mosque to Al Qasba canal entrance. The engaging illuminated Gobo art projections by the emirate's artistic youth gives you an insight into Sharjah’s youngsters’ creative talents!\n\nKalba Clock Tower\n\nOne of Sharjah’s newest attractions decorated in lights for the first time; viewers enjoy the unique audio-visual narrative display, especially in the ‘blue hour’. The tower stuns in an atmospheric show with augmented visual reality, mixed with dynamic music, enhancing the festive mood.\n\nSharjah Mosque\n\nThe largest mosque in Sharjah attracts a huge number of visitors every year! The laser show enhances the rich architectural beauty of the mosque, with different color themes. The crystalline visual design of the color pattern and vibrant artistic expression makes the user enter a creative mode and explore the aspects of the light techniques.\n\nAnd much more..\n\nIn addition to these stunning, light displays, the festival also features a range of cultural events and activities, including music performances, theater shows, and workshops for children. These events offer visitors a unique opportunity to learn about the rich cultural heritage and ethnic architectural design of Sharjah.\n\nThe event also invites photographers and art lovers to take part in a special competition hosted by SCTDA to win prizes.\n\nBuildings and mosques came alive for 12 nights straight as the Sharjah Light Festival painted the Emirate in a hue of colours. The 12th edition of the festival, which ended on February 19, saw 600 employees, workers, and volunteers come together to put on breath-taking displays at 13 locations.\nPlanning for the event began in December 2022, with the shows seeing the light in a “record time” of three months, a top official told Khaleej Times.\n“The 2023 festival welcomed seven international artists, along with a group of emerging ones,” said Khalid Jasim Al Midfa, Chairman of the Sharjah Commerce and Tourism Development Authority (SCTDA).\nFrom February 8 to 19, cold nights lit up as mosques like Al Noor, Sharjah and Sheikh Rashid bin Ahmed Al Qasimi; and heritage sites like Sharjah Fort (Al Hisn), Al Rafisah Dam and Kalba Clock Tower, and other locations across the Emirate, basked in the warmth of stunning projections. Lights formed characters that told stories to the tune of epic orchestral music.\n“The Sharjah Light Festival presented shows and performances inspired by the traditional heritage of the Emirate of Sharjah, the geometry, motifs, calligraphy, and patterns of Arab and Islamic architecture that characterise its landmarks,” Al Midfa said. “The Emirate of Sharjah has a distinctive architectural character, and its monuments and buildings have engineering details that reflect its identity and culture.”\nA special committee chose the locations to highlight the “aesthetics and details” of the architecture and designs.\n\n“When selecting sites, we are keen to ensure they are in harmony with the light shows and accompanying music, which reveal the subtle details of these buildings, and highlight the originality of Sharjah and its position as a hub for Islamic architecture, arts, and calligraphy,” added Al Midfa.\nSaying it with lights\nThe shows shed light on scenes from the Emirate’s journey, “which reflect the advancements made in various fields such as education, arts, environment, history, science, and others”. The displays also outline perceptions for a bright future, added Al Midfa.\n\n“The performances focus on the impact of art in the world and its place in the future, and the role of both culture and knowledge in overcoming the difficulties and challenges that face the nations of the world.”", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [4021, 264, 220, 17, 15, 15, 15, 4244, 4549, 7517, 1663, 4549, 323, 3321, 4079, 519, 419, 448, 220, 16, 15, 15, 4, 902, 83898, 323, 4911, 715, 42215, 97396, 8658, 17322, 374, 279, 10951, 2393, 315, 13498, 220, 17, 15, 17, 18, 4894, 42215, 97396, 594, 6930, 12752, 3100, 18780, 374, 1182, 369, 1181, 220, 16, 17, 339, 1042, 2928, 362, 2409, 9775, 1538, 5644, 304, 279, 46849, 11, 312, 28016, 5740, 279, 3283, 1119, 264, 33866, 3037, 315, 3100, 323, 4627, 13, 1096, 1042, 594, 18780, 3855, 389, 13498, 220, 23, 323, 374, 50547, 9037, 315, 15255, 3941, 678, 5313, 1361, 11, 15245, 382, 37666, 1280, 4142, 7186, 5440, 11, 10693, 369