INFO 03-28 14:00:51 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-6c5b5709c477408ebc8c17c4eb610f0e-0: prompt: 'These are 8 Hooks for Videos You Can Use to Grab Your Audience\'s Attention\n1. Start With a Fascinating Fact.\n2. What If…\n3. Surprise Them.\n4. In Medias Res.\n5. Start With a Problem & Offer a Solution.\n6. Open With a Joke.\n7. Ask a Question.\n8. Hint at a Story\n\nUse each of these 8 suggestions to write me 8 different YouTube video hooks for my video based on my video notes below. Each hook should be 2 paragraphs long.\n\n"Did you know that most teachings in the church today regarding the roles of men and women are based on the curse of sin and not God’s original intention? Did you know that Jesus died to put us in a position to have the original Life God gifted Adam and Eve and yet, most of us are being taught – in church - to live according to the curse of sin? \n\n- God created Adam and helped him realize he needed a companion that is comparable to him\n- blessed Adam and Eve together and God commanded them to have dominion over the earth\n- God didn’t bless Adam alone, and the enemy never attacked Adam alone\n- once Eve showed up and God blessed them, that’s when the enemy attacked them: the serpent focused on twisting God’s Word and creating doubt about the Goodness of God and His Intentions, not the actual fruit\n- then they sin\n- God comes into the Garden and gives them an opportunity to take responsibility for their sins individually, but they fall deeper into sin instead by blaming the other person for their personal choice to act against the Word of God\n\nSlide 1:\nGenesis 3:17-19: Then to Adam He said, “Because you have heeded the voice of your wife, and have eaten from the tree of which I commanded you, saying, ‘You shall not eat of it’:\n\n“Cursed is the ground for your sake;\nIn toil you shall eat of it\nAll the days of your life.\nBoth thorns and thistles it shall bring forth for you,\nAnd you shall eat the herb of the field.\nIn the sweat of your face you shall eat bread\nTill you return to the ground,\nFor out of it you were taken;\nFor dust you are,\nAnd to dust you shall return.”\n\n- and most church teachings say men’s main purpose is to work because of a distortion of the enemy about this Scripture:\n\nSlide 2:\n1 Timothy 5:8: But if anyone does not provide for his own, and especially for those of his household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever.\n\n- if we read the whole chapter though, he is very clear this is not in any way referring to men working at women staying at home, at all:\n\nSlide 3:\n1 Timothy 5:16: If any believing man or woman has widows, let them relieve them, and do not let the church be burdened, that it may relieve those who are really widows.\n\n- Jesus teaches us that we need to \\*always look at the context of the whole Bible in order to understand what each Commandment means\n- in the wilderness, the enemy attacked Jesus with Scriptures taken out of context – that’s what he does\n- he doesn’t try to get us to believe something wild, he comes at us with God’s Word but a distortion of it that God never intended for us to believe or do and doing it is a sin\n\n- women are meant to work and a working, skilled wife has always been desirable – even in the Old Testament they understood this\n\n- another thing we need to understand is this: men and husbands are commanded to raise their children, even starting with the Old Testament:\n\nSlide 4:\nDeuteronomy 6:6-9: “And these words which I command you today shall be in your heart. You shall teach them diligently to your children, and shall talk of them when you sit in your house, when you walk by the way, when you lie down, and when you rise up. You shall bind them as a sign on your hand, and they shall be as frontlets between your eyes. You shall write them on the doorposts of your house and on your gates.\n\n- this Commandment was given to both mothers and fathers, from the very beginning and Jesus came to bring us together, not separate us\n\nSlide 5:\nEphesians 6:4: And you, fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath, but bring them up in the training and admonition of the Lord.\n\n- this is a clear Commandment to fathers in specific to bring their children up in the training and admonition of the Lord\n\n- but the enemy has distorted these Commandments making men and women think they are doing God’s Will if men work and women stay at home\n- here’s what Jesus says:\n\nSlide 6:\nMatthew 12:25: But Jesus knew their thoughts, and said to them: “Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation, and every city or house divided against itself will not stand.\n\n- men are at work, doing everything themselves, women are at home, doing everything themselves\n- satan has separated men and women\n- women are not fulfilling their God-given role and assigment to be helpers and help men in everything, but satan has lied to us saying this is what God wants\n- we are divided – we have split life in two parts, and we are alone dealing with each part\n- God never intended for that, but it’s up to us to believe Him and not the enemy\n\n- think of it: men being the providers means women are codependent on men – if my husband doesn’t work, I don’t have money to live. I am at the mercy of my husband\n- women raising the children means men are codependent on women – without my wife there, I don’t know how to interact with my children\n- sure, there is the Grace of God on all of us, and some people are naturally talented in these things, but we need to remember we are all meant to become more like Jesus and He both worked (as a carpenter) and interacted with children"', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logpr