INFO 03-28 14:01:23 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-a21cc737959a4689ba3f0aec562ca84a-0: prompt: 'I am interviewing for Zipline Logistics, and I am giving you the Job Description as a Prompt:\n\n am giving you Sample Questions on Two Topics:\nTopic One: Technical System Design\nTopic Two: Take Home Challenge and Code\n\nBased on the questions below, create 10 questions for Topic One and 10 questions for Topic Two in the context of Zipline Logistics:\n\nContext Keywords: Zipline, Drones, Delivery, Logistics, Flights, Packages, Storage, Inventory, Machine, Analytics, Apps that calculate the movement of the Drones, Returing of Drones Back to System, Charging of Drones, Health Supplies, Orders\n\nDesign a temporary system to be used in the management and scheduling of propeller replacements which currently are only usable up to 50 flights, until the engineering team can finish and incorporate the replacements which last much longer."\n\nSystem Design: "Here\'s a list of all the issues in our backlog. Please prioritize them and talk about how you would approach solving them."\n\nTechnical System Design and Take Home: brainstorm a design/solution to a situation pertaining to Zipline\'s drones.\nTake Home Challenge: Create a Program that Estimates the Battery Life of Drones in Zipline Logistics with multiple variables.\n\nTechnical System Design: Design a system to order with low connectivity\nTopic One: Technical System Design\n\nDesign a system for monitoring and managing the inventory levels of replacement parts for Zipline\'s drones.\nDevelop a system for scheduling and coordinating drone flights for maximum efficiency and minimal downtime.\nCreate a system for tracking and analyzing drone performance data to optimize flight patterns and improve delivery times.\nDesign a system for monitoring and regulating the charging of drones to ensure they are always ready for their next flight.\nDevelop a system for managing the storage and distribution of health supplies using Zipline\'s drones.\nCreate a system for managing and allocating resources for the repair and maintenance of Zipline\'s drones.\nDesign a system for tracking and managing the movement of Zipline\'s drones in real-time.\nDevelop a system for predicting and preventing potential flight risks and hazards to Zipline\'s drones.\nCreate a system for monitoring and controlling the returning of drones to the system.\nDesign a system for integrating analytics and machine learning to improve the overall performance of Zipline\'s drone logistics operation.\nTopic Two: Take Home Challenge and Code\n\nWrite a program that tracks the number of flights a propeller replacement can handle before needing to be replaced.\nCreate a program that calculates the estimated delivery time for a package based on current flight patterns and drone performance data.\nDevelop a program that optimizes the charging schedule of Zipline\'s drones to ensure they are always ready for their next flight.\nWrite a program that predicts potential flight risks and hazards for Zipline\'s drones.\nCreate a program that tracks the movement and location of Zipline\'s drones in real-time.\nDevelop a program that manages the inventory levels of replacement parts for Zipline\'s drones.\nWrite a program that optimizes the scheduling and coordination of drone flights for maximum efficiency.\nCreate a program that estimates the battery life of drones in Zipline Logistics with multiple variables.\nDevelop a program that manages the storage and distribution of health supplies using Zipline\'s drones.\nWrite a program that predicts and prevents potential flight risks and hazards to Zipline\'s drones.\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION:\nI am providing you the Job Description of Zipline\'s "Software Engineering - Full Stack Apps" Role.\nHowever, I am interviewing for the "Software Apps Intern" role, which is more for New Graduates and University going students.\n\nHowever, I lost the Job Description of the Software Apps Intern role.\n\nBased on the following description, create the Job Description of the Intern role for me.\n\nSWE - Full Stack Apps Job Description:\nAbout Zipline\nDo you want to change the world? Zipline is on a mission to transform the way goods move. Our aim is to solve the world’s most urgent and complex access challenges by building, manufacturing and operating the first instant delivery and logistics system that serves all humans equally, wherever they are. From powering Rwanda’s national blood delivery network and Ghana’s COVID-19 vaccine distribution, to providing on-demand home delivery for Walmart, to enabling healthcare providers to bring care directly to U.S. homes, we are transforming the way things move for businesses, governments and consumers.\n \nThe technology is complex but the idea is simple: a teleportation service that delivers what you need, when you need it. Through our technology that includes robotics and autonomy, we are decarbonizing delivery, decreasing road congestion, and reducing fossil fuel consumption and air pollution, while providing equitable access to billions of people and building a more resilient global supply chain.\n \nJoin Zipline and help us to make good on our promise to build an equitable and more resilient global supply chain for billions of people.\nAbout You and The Role \nZipline is expanding our autonomous drone delivery network around the world, helping people get what they need, no matter where they live. Our software team builds applications and services that power our fleet operations, our warehouse operations, tools for integrating with partners, and apps for our customers to place orders on-demand.\n\nWe’re looking for expert software engineers that love shipping great product at fast pace to a truly global audience. This ranges from ordering portals for pharmacists, to inventory APIs to integrate with our partners, to Android apps for healthcare workers in the field. The role includes development across the full-stack of our codebase. The role is end-to-end in the product life cycle, from ideation and requirements gathering, through system design, implementation, validation, and rollout.\n\nWhat You\'ll Do \nYou’ll build ownership for understanding and solving a core customer’s problems, for example:\n\nImprove our Air Traffic Control application that gives our regulators real-time oversight of our fleet\nDesign a dependable system for doctors and nurses to order life-saving supplies from Zipline, regardless of their internet connectivity\nEmpower our fulfillment teams with amazing software tools to track inventory, process orders, prepare aircraft, and monitor flight status\nOwn applications and services end-to-end\nMentor fellow engineers\nShip high-impact functionality on a monthly basis\nWhat You\'ll Bring \n8+ years experience in software engineering\n4+ years experience providing technical leadership to cross-team initiatives\nExpertise in modern web languages, technologies, and best practices \nExperience architecting and deploying a system of web services\nExperience designing software for security, scalability, and reliability\nExperience designing third-party APIs, nuanced ontologies, and sophisticated data models\nStrong product instincts and empathy for the customer\nSoftware Apps Intern Job Description:\n\nAbout Zipline:\nDo you want to change the world? Zipline is on a mission to transform the way goods move. Our aim is to solve the world’s most urgent and complex access challenges by building, manufacturing and operating the first instant delivery and logistics system that serves all humans equally, wherever they are. From powering Rwanda’s national blood delivery network and Ghana’s COVID-19 vaccine distribution, to providing on-demand home delivery for Walmart, to enabling healthcare providers to bring care directly to U.S. homes, we are transforming the way things move for businesses, governments and consumers.\n\nAbout the Role:\nAs a Software Apps Intern at Zipline, you will have the opportunity to work with a team of expert software engineers in building applications and services that power our fleet operations, our warehouse operations, tools for integrating with partners, and apps for our customers to place orders on-demand. You will be responsible for end-to-end in the product life cycle, from ideation and requirements gathering, through system design, implementation, validation, and rollout.\n\nWhat You\'ll Do:\n\nYou’ll work on a project with the team to understand and solve a core customer’s problems.\nYou\'ll learn to design a dependable system for doctors and nurses to order life-saving supplies from Zipline, regardless of their internet connectivity\nYou\'ll learn to empower our fulfillment teams with amazing software tools to track inventory, process orders, prepare aircraft, and monitor flight status\nYou\'ll learn to own applications and services end-to-end\nYou\'ll learn to ship high-impact functionality on a monthly basis\nWhat You\'ll Bring:\n\nCurrently enrolled in a Computer Science or related field of study\nStrong knowledge in modern web languages, technologies, and best practices\nStrong product instincts and empathy for the customer\nStrong problem-solving and analytical skills\nStrong communication skills\nStrong sense of responsibility\nStrong desire to learn and continuously improve\nThis role is an entry-level position and is an ideal opportunity for new graduates and university students looking to gain practical experience in software engineering and to work with a team of experts in delivering cutting-edge technology for a global audience.\n\nWhat You\'ll Do:\n\nAssist in building and maintaining software applications and services that power Zipline\'s fleet operations, warehouse operations, and tools for integrating with partners\nCollaborate with the software team to improve our Air Traffic Control application that gives our regulators real-time oversight of our fleet\nWork on designing a dependable system for doctors and nurses to order life-saving supplies from Zipline, regardless of their internet connectivity\nContribute to the development and improvement of software tools to track inventory, process orders, prepare aircraft, and monitor flight status\nLearn and assist with the end-to-end product life cycle, from ideation and requirements gathering, through system design, implementation, validation, and rollout\nGain mentorship from experienced engineers and work on high-impact functionality on a monthly basis\nLearn and develop skills in modern web languages, technologies, and best practices\nGet hands-on experience in software development and learn about software design for security, scalability, and reliability\nLearn about designing third-party APIs, nuanced ontologies, and sophisticated data models\nDevelop strong product instincts and empathy for the customer.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [40, 1079, 64716, 369, 1863, 47429, 70322, 11, 323, 358, 1079, 7086, 498, 279, 12011, 7662, 438, 264, 59501, 1447, 1079, 7086, 498, 19143, 23382, 389, 9043, 40894, 510, 26406, 3776, 25, 26668, 739, 6982, 198, 26406, 9043, 25, 11778, 5379, 25257, 323, 6119, 271, 28715, 389, 279, 4755, 3685, 11, 1855, 220, 16, 15, 4755, 369, 32911, 3776, 323, 220, 16, 15, 4755, 369, 32911, 9043, 304, 279, 2266, 315, 1863, 47429, 70322, 1447, 1972, 55695, 25, 1863, 47429, 11, 422, 31821, 11, 26211, 11, 70322, 11, 2988, 2796, 11, 63384, 11, 14693, 11, 28126, 11, 12960, 11, 32427, 11, 33020, 429, 11047, 279, 7203, 315, 279, 422, 31821, 11, 10392, 1677,