INFO 03-28 14:01:32 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-a53b6f2176c84402a25112f053af8a5b-0: prompt: "Write a YouTube for men ages 18-49 script based on this draft: Does GOD exist?\n\nI’m going to throw out a possible reason why one might not believe in God, but it is a red herring (something that misleads or distracts from the relevant question) does God exist? \n\nTo answer this question I am going to give you a “red herring” so I’m going to distract you with something that misleads you from answer the question: does God Exist.\n\nHere is an example of a Red Herring and you will hear someone say you can live a good and charitable life without God.” \n\nThat’s a red herring. I did not answer the question whether God exists, but I demonstrated a preconceived notion that the question about the existence of God implies a human response to God. \n\nI’ll show you another one and this is a red herring in response to the question does God exist?\n\n“The false God’s of many religions are not true God’s.” \n\nAgain, I’m not answer the question whether God exists, but I’m pointing out that there are many false God’s.\n\nAnother reason to deny the existence of God is to point all the horrible things that people have done in the name of their so-called, “God” to somehow detract from the question of God’s existence.\n\nLastly, you have may have heard this red herring about the words of Scriptures that they are not reliable and you cannot trust religious institutions especially organized religion.\n\nNow that we’ve covered just a few red herrings let me know in the comments below what red herrings you have heard of when it comes to that fateful question whether God exists? \n\nYou’ll notice what most red herrings have in common is this theme: “that you will not Lord over me.” This is the predominate theme of the red-hearings. It is true that in our culture and our world today because we are aware of the many religions and so-called god’s that most people are familiar at least a little bit with what the implication is if God exists. Essentially, baked into the question, “Does God exist?” Is the presupposition that if God does exist then which God do you believe in because there are many gods according to history of humanity. If the question “Does God Exist?” Is actually answer with “yes” or a “no” then of course the next question is “Why?” If you say yes then you have to explain why it is that you believe God exists and likewise if no you have to explain why. Inevitably, if the answer is yes then the person who believes that God exists must act according to that belief. The question of how one acts according to that belief is entirely up to the individual. Just because someone believes that God exist does not mean that they are religious in any way. Someone can say yes God exists, but what they mean by that could be anything and they might even think that they are God. \n\nand religion.” Now, let’s not get ahead of ourselves this is a red herring because the question is; does God exist? I’m not saying that everyone will answer this question does God exist in this way. I’m not surprised when this question, “why do I need God to be a good person?” Is assumed in relation to the question does God exist? I’m going to offer this up to you in the comments below that very question and I want you to do your very best to tell me and everyone else if God exists.\n\nI want you to tell me if God exists. And I don’t want you to tell me about religion or being a good person. Only answer the question. Does God exist and I want to see if despite the temptations we can discuss only that question, so stick to the basics without getting into religion or what it means to know God or believe in God and what that entails, but just answer the question Does God exist and you have to explain why you believe God exists or that God does not exist. That is the question does God exist and if so why do you believe God exists? Leave your answers below and try to keep it brief so like maybe in 100 words or less. No more than a brief paragraph. How do you know that God exists or does not exist put your answers below.\n\nNow, let us begin to consider that if God exists then we have to have a reason why God has to exist. We cannot believe that God exists merely by some human default that something must exist to explain all of the cosmos because it is possible to imagine that existence always exists. That is not to say that our universe always existed because that does not appears so rather it seems to have an age of approximately 13.8 billion years. Let us just say that there was a time when the universe did exist as we know it, so how it existed prior to existence is a bit of non-sequitur theoretically because nothing can exist prior to itself. You did not exist prior to conception; there was time when you did not exist. There was a time when human beings, people were not. The earth was not, the stars were not there were no planets non time space continuum just existence itself whatever that is. Something we know not what exist and the reason we can know that something must have existed prior to all of the universe is primarily because it, you and all of this exists. You have heard, “I think therefore I am,” is the first principle of René Descartes's philosophy. I am able to think therefore I exist; now let us go back to the beginning before the universe exist. Is it possible that nothing exist. Is there such a thing as non-existent? Yes, in terms of the universe itself because it was non-existent; it did not exist. Whatever existed was not the universe, so you can be certain that whatever pre-existed the universe is existence itself. Why? Why does existence need to exist; why does the universe exist because it exists and to exist means it is as Descarte said, “I think therefore I am.” I exist, but there was a time when I did not exist, so existence even prior to the universe itself must have existed. Otherwise, we and the universe itself could not exist. In otherwords how can anything exist if existence does not exist. Existence must precede all that is in existence. To exercise the act of existence is what St. Thomas Aquinas said, was that “a thing cannot be unless it possesses an act of being” right “I think therefore I am,” I am an act of being. Go all the way back before all the universe existed is it possible that nothing could have existed or did existence exist? Another way of putting this might be to ask you the question can you exist without existing; you can’t; you cannot exist and not exist at the same time, but also you cannot exist prior to your own existence yet you exist. Same with the universe it did not exist before it existed, so then where did it come from; did it come from? It exists, so existence must exist without material existence. \n\nI can demonstrate this for you. Imagine that nothing exists. You have to imagine nothing, but you can’t do that because your imagination can only imagine something. You cannot imagine nothing; you don’t even know what nothing is. It’s impossible to imagine nothing; you can’t; it’s not possible. To imagine is to imagine something, so you cannot imagine a time even outside of time and matter before it all. You can’t imagine that it’s not possible because to imagine is to exist to think and so you do it. Just speaking is enough to know that you cannot think without imagining something. You cannot escape existence; even in your sleep you dream; you may not remember, but even in your sleep your mind is working; it’s existing. When you die your mind no longer exists in your body, and I would argue it still exists along with your will, so you rmind and will is your soul and it exists after your body dies, but were are not going to go there. We are sticking with your mind because there was a time when it did not exist, but you cannot imagine that because is impossible for your mind to imagine its own non-existence. You just can’t do it primarily because it exists, but there was a time when it did not. You can understand what Descarte is saying, “I think… therefore… I am.” It makes sense because after all if I”m thinking then I must exist, but I know there was a time when I did not exist, but I cannot imagine what it was like not to exist. Existence cannot imagine non-existence. When you really think about it Descarte was little bit backwards in this thinking because he does not exist because he thinks; he thinks because he exists. Listen one more time. If I say I think there I am I have it backwards; it’s actually I am, I exist therefore I think. My existence is not preceded by my thinking; I can’t think before I exist and I don’t exit because I think. I think because I exist; existence comes first before thinking. Now, think about that if you exist before you think that means you existed before you could think about existing, but there was a time when you did not exist. You were made; there was a point in human history when you came into existence, but you did not come into existence out of nothing and nor did you say I exist because I think nor I think therefore I am. Never were you more confused about your existence until Descarte came up with this radical idea about, “thinking therefore I am.” This is like saying I think we are living in a simulation and I don’t know if any of this is real; I am real; do I exist. No we don’t really ask that question in practical life we accept the fact that we exist whether we think about it or not. \n\nLet us go back to what another philosopher said, “a thing cannot be unless it possesses an act of being.” This is Aquinas. What does this mean; it means, “to be or not to be is not the question, because to be is to be; to exist is to exist. It’s not that complicated; you either exist or you don’t exist. Earth exists or it does not exist. Space exist or it does not. The Universe; same. What if the universe does not exist then the question is does existence exist; does anything exist. A pure materialist would say that nothing exists because the only thing that exists is material that’s it al energy is material, all negative energy is material; it’s all material everything that there is nothing behind the material universe. For the materialist when the universe did not exist nothing existed. But you have to ask yourself if this is even possible because if there was a time when nothing existed; nothing; is that possible? Is it possible for nothing to exist? Remember, to exist is something; just existence itself is existence. I’m not rendering a God here to say somehow that God is just existence. I’m just saying do you even think it is possible for things to exist without existence existing first that’s all. I’m just saying that something must have existed before the universe otherwise how else could existence exist there was no such thing as existence before all of the universe existed. I can also demonstrate this for you by saying everything in our world exists and everything in our universe exists no take all that matter and make it not exist. Put the genie back int he bottle, so to speak, put it all back inside the big bang before it went off before it came into existence. There was a time when there were no planets, stars/suns, moons etc. That stuff did not exist at one point according to science, so if all this matter like so much matter you don’t even know what to do with put it all inside of a tiny little pinhead, but a million, trillion, gazillion times smaller that it doesn’t even exist. You don’t think a God exists? Cram all that material into non-existence; literally make existence not exist; try that; you can’t do it because otherwise nothing could exist.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_to