INFO 03-28 14:03:10 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-1488cfe44da7460a9876e07300489f7b-0: prompt: 'CHAPTER NINE\n\n\nCOMMUNITY BUILDING & MANAGEMENT\n\nWhat Are Online Communities?\nBuilding an online community is becoming an increasingly important component of digital\nmarketing strategies, regardless of the size of your company or the scope of your brand\'s reach.\nIn the real world, communities serve as the bedrock upon which contemporary society is\nbuilt. They o er a support system and facilitate the exchange of information. We humans\nare social creatures by nature, and we have a tendency to feel more secure when we are\nparticipating in activities that involve other people. When things get di cult, communities\nstep up to o er assistance, advice, and rst-hand experience, and as a result, a strong\nbond is formed between individuals from a wide variety of walks of life. It is important not\nto undervalue the in uence that can be exerted by a group when its members unite\naround a common purpose or interest and work toward a common goal.\nEmpowering groups of people to collaborate and communicate online are online\ncommunities such as Facebook groups, forums, and hashtags. Online communities could\nbe the secret to your success on the internet, whether it\'s through connecting with others\nover a common interest or following a well-known brand on social media. You can\nposition your business and brand as an industry leader by tapping into online\ncommunities or by forming your own digital group. This will allow you to create a section\nof the internet where your brand provides information, advice, support, tips, resolutions,\nanswers, and entertainment. Within this miniature world of the internet, it is in your power\nto turn users into devoted customers.\nThe question that needs to be answered is which member of your team will volunteer to\ntake on this new role.\n\n\nThe Importance of Community Management\n\nYou need to be a real person in order to have an authentic social voice for your brand,\nand part of being a real person involves spending some time online from time to time.\nBelieve us when we say that striking a healthy balance in the always-on world of social\nmedia will make you a better community manager and a better person overall.\nYour company has an obligation to maintain and grow its online community if it has a\nsizeable following on any of the social media platforms. When a client contacts you, you\nneed to show interest, be responsive, and take appropriate action. Authentic responses\nand engagement are proven to generate more brand loyalty than a generic presence\never could. This is where the role of a community manager comes into play, as they must\ncompletely immerse themselves in the company and personify the tone of voice and\nvalues that are associated with the brand.\nThey will wear the face of your company while implementing new ways to engage with\nyour community online, bringing a human element to your social media groups, and will\ndo so while wearing the face of your company. It is helpful to provide them with their own\nbranded social media pro les (that are distinct from the accounts used for your business),\nas this gives them a link to your brand without making them appear to be an employee of\nyour company. You can shake up your social media strategy and see the bene ts by\npaving the way for a more playful and relatable approach to social media marketing. This\nwill allow you to reap the bene ts of shaking up your social media strategy.\nNow that we have that out of the way, let\'s look at all the ways adding a community manager to your team will bene t you.\n\n\n\nBene ts of Hiring a Community Manager\n\nSave time and avoid negative customer reviews by managing and responding to online\ncustomer enquiries, questions, and complaints.\nGain insight into the lives of your online audience to help tailor your digital marketing strategy.\nOnline, connect with other brands and in uencers to form exciting collaborations. Obtain valuable insight into your online customers\' honest opinions about your brand, product, or service.\nHave a real person representing you online with whom customers can connect and respond.\nCreating and maintaining an online community can not only help your company save and\ngenerate more money in the long run, but it will also save your company a signi cant\namount of time in the short term. Online communities provide businesses with the\nopportunity to gain insight into their consumers\' thought processes, which may do\neverything from bolstering a company\'s trustworthiness and legitimacy to facilitating the\ndevelopment of more data-driven business decisions. Therefore, as an alternative to\nmaking an investment in pay-per-click advertisements to drive tra c to your product\npages, you can instead choose to answer questions relating to the industry, post advice\nand tips to your online audience, and develop an organic community that is interested in\nyour brand and business.\n\nHow Community Management Will Transform Digital Marketing\n\nThe question is, how exactly will community managers take over the function of ordinary\nsocial media marketers?\nDespite the fact that "engagement" has been a buzzword in the world of digital marketing\nfor the past couple of years, there are still some brands that have not quite mastered\n"engagement optimization," which entails investing the appropriate amount of time,\nenergy, and resources into being present in the moment. Even though it can be a time-\nconsuming process to respond to everyone online, making this e ort will help you create\nbrand awareness and loyalty through the cultivation of online communities.\n\nAdapt Your Social Media Strategy\n\nThe use of social media platforms has developed into an essential component of modern\nliving. It is the place where we catch up with friends and family, where we can release our\nfrustrations, and where we can share our experiences, top suggestions, and advise with\none another. The use of social media as a tool to listen to and keep track of the actions of\nusers is an extremely useful strategy for businesses that want to develop deeper\nrelationships with the clients they serve online. It is the most e ective platform to analyze\nmentions of a brand, to strengthen customer loyalty to a company, and to reward customers with special o ers.\nCommunity management is an innovative strategy to digital marketing that will focus on\nthe cultivation of online communities while simultaneously o ering analysis, information,\ncustomer support, and creative material in real time. A social media manager will spend\ntime scheduling content to go live across various platforms at the best times of the day.\nOn the other hand, a community manager\'s role will involve being ready on the social\nmedia frontline to respond, reply, comment, and share information at the drop of a hat\nwhenever it is needed.\nWhat\'s the takeaway here? The management of online communities is an essential\ncomponent of providing customer care online. This new approach to social media\nmarketing will focus on developing trust, increasing brand recognition, and being\ntransparent in order to break down barriers that previously existed between companies,\nbrands, and online customers. It is absolutely essential to cultivate leads, advance clients\nfurther through the sales funnel, and prioritize the satisfaction of existing customers. And\nbecause information is power, the degree to which your clients are well educated will\ndirectly correlate to the likelihood that they will make an investment in your brand.\n\nUnlock The Power Of Community Management\n\nThe world of social media is showing no signs of slowing down, and this holds true\nregardless of whether you post on Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, Reddit, LinkedIn, or\nTikTok. As a professional in business or digital marketing, the thought of having to manage\nyour online presence while simultaneously being relevant, responsive, on-trend, and\nengaging across all platforms might feel overwhelming. However, there are many\ne ective strategies to manage your online presence.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [87439, 451, 3981, 1406, 55554, 56173, 47697, 1718, 609, 93278, 271, 3838, 8713, 8105, 57343, 5267, 30133, 458, 2860, 3942, 374, 10454, 458, 14756, 2989, 3692, 315, 7377, 198, 91818, 14830, 11, 15484, 315, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 2813, 476, 279, 6891, 315, 697, 6741, 594, 5545, 624, 641, 279, 1931, 1879, 11, 10744, 8683, 438, 279, 4845, 20521, 5193, 892, 18706, 8232, 374, 198, 46239, 13, 2379, 297, 2714, 264, 1824, 1849, 323, 27596, 279, 9289, 315, 1995, 13, 1205, 12677, 198, 546, 3590, 19970, 553, 6993, 11, 323, 582, 614, 264, 30854, 311, 2666, 803, 9767, 979, 582, 525, 198, 4480, 8442, 1095, 304, 7488, 429, 21058, 1008, 1251, 13, 3197, 2513, 633, 1853, 4511, 11, 10744, 198, 9520, 705, 311, 297, 2714, 12994, 11, 9462, 11, 323, 55515, 24413, 3139, 11, 323, 438, 264, 1102, 11, 264, 3746, 198, 64239, 374, 14122, 1948, 7775, 504, 264, 6884, 8045, 315, 22479, 315, 2272, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 537, 198, 983, 2030, 648, 540, 279, 304, 575, 763, 429, 646, 387, 42744, 291, 553, 264, 1874, 979, 1181, 3613, 51596, 198, 19454, 264, 4185, 7428, 476, 2734, 323, 975, 8841, 264, 4185, 5795, 624, 28731, 89614, 5203, 315, 1251, 311, 50596, 323, 19032, 2860, 525, 2860, 198, 3621, 6037, 1741, 438, 5573, 5203, 11, 24865, 11, 323, 81861, 13, 8105, 10744, 1410, 198, 1371, 279, 6234, 311, 697, 2393, 389, 279, 7602, 11, 3425, 432, 594, 1526,