INFO 03-28 14:03:25 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-41c0a0ca9bcd4ea2bc6a846b9555ad5d-0: prompt: "Correct spelling and grammar, and turn this into a script for an inviting video for a luxxurious 6 bedroom 5 bedroom mansion that also serves as a filmset locationa and company offsite office space or event space for baby showers, health and wellness events and more. \n\nPart 1 \n\nAlright, so here's a tour of 215 North Hollywood Way in Burbank, California 91505.\n\nAka the Chateau Chichie, spelled CHA, T, A, EAU, A.\n\nThe Chateau Chichie, spelled CHA, T, A, EAU, CHICHI.\n\nSo the Chateau Chichie is spelled CHA.\n\nT-A-U-C-H-I-C-H-I.\n\nSo starting from the front on Hollywood Way, North Hollywood Way, you're EAUCHI So starting from the front on Hollywood Way, North Hollywood Way, we entered the white wall.\n\nthe little black door through the white wall.\n\nYou see a three-story house with double sliding windows on the left side and a closed facade on the right side of the front facade.\n\nEntering through the front you walk kind of to the side of the house through this little walkway that brings you to the main entrance which is a large sliding door where there's four panels and the two middle panels slide open.\n\nYou enter a hallway that is very unconventional or unusual for a hallway.\n\nYou immediately see that the border between inside and outside has kind of been blurred or even erased by the clever addition of astroturf inside so you have indoor astroturf and then white marble rolled rock so rolled white marble landscaping rock on the edges and a large concrete cylinder planter pot with in there a sculpture of a real eucalyptus tree with branches sticking out like a real tree and on the branches are fresh cut eucalyptus branches that the designer got at the market so that there's a natural perfume of eucalyptus, fresh eucalyptus inside the hallway.\n\nSo that's already an immediate signature scent of the house fresh eucalyptus you look to your left and you see a large 10-foot cactus and four neon coral colored wire mesh stools for guests to sit and hang out or wait for their uber or lift or or what have you or just to grace the space.\n\nSo there's a double staircase as you look into the house from the main entrance.\n\nSo there's one staircase that goes to the left and one staircase that goes to the right.\n\nSo there is also the ground floor.\n\nwhich consists of the middle hallway that you're standing in and then on the left side so the east side of the house the front side of the house which is the street side of North Hollywood Way that side you you go through a little hallway that consists of AstroTurf and the same landscaping rug and That hallway I as the designer call it the hallway of innovation the the gallery of trailblazers or the the the hallway that is an ode to trailblazers and innovators and and inventors and entrepreneurs so for example you have a 1908 Aircraft propeller made from wood that is hanging on the wall.\n\nIt's about 10 feet long and You know that is like an invention that changed the world and you can see the little detail on the propellers the the bolts and The nuts that were used back in those days were still square.\n\nThey didn't even have the hexagon nuts and bolts yet so I Think that was really cool then there's also a Picture of Rosa Parks the civil rights pioneer and trailblazer who.\n\nIs most famously known for opposing the segregation on the bus and the resulting bus boycott from the civil rights movement.\n\nAlso a very important trailblazer and then you also have pictures of framed copies of Life magazine from the 1960s when mankind was conquering the moon.\n\nA little bit further down the hallway you enter a gallery space which could be seen as a studio that has its own kitchenette.\n\nIt has a huge walnut boardroom table that can seat comfortably 15 people.\n\nThere is also a display table with object are object that as they say like artifacts it can be modified it can be changed to exhibit different kinds of items there's art on the walls and there is one modern abstract piece of art on plexiglass of wooden cubes in bright pastel colors each side of each cube is different bright colors so as a colorful addition in the middle of the room stands currently a 2016 Harley Davidson special edition limited edition the same one that was driven by Bradley Cooper in the movie stars born which is also the same motorcycle that was used for the upcoming feature documentary made by empty factory about Jason Esterhausen the movie is called or the documentary is called blind writer it's a feature documentary following the exploits of Jason a blind man from South Africa who is on a quest to set a world record of fastest speed on a motorcycle by a blind person so the there's a TV on the wall that can be used for business meetings board meetings, events, gallery openings and so on.\n\nThere is a TV that is currently playing the trailer to the feature documentary about Blind Rider and then there is a ample closet space also in the hallway there's a large closet space that can house at least 50 jackets at minimum probably a hundred so that's a cloakroom and then on the opposite side of the cloakroom in the middle of this little hallway there is the ground floor bathroom which is a large bathroom has a bathtub as well as a standing shower and a large freestanding bathroom vanity with nice finishes luxury faucet and finishes as as well as a toilet.\n\nBack down the hallway through past the tree again, you go straight to find the garage.\n\nIn the garage we have a number of special edition vintage motorcycles like the Euro sidecar motorcycle very good prop for photography we have a brand new Husqvarna 501S Duosport Enduro motocross bike we have a KTM Duosport Touring bike and also Sun A Ducati Monster 2004 and a 1985 Moto Goodsy Le Mans L E M A N S the garage also has astroturf, a workbench, toolkits and all the power tools that you could ever want It fits two cars in the current setup with the motorcycles it fits one car.\n\nThe garage can be accessed from the back alley which is the same number and the same street.\n\nIt's also called 215 North Hollywood Way.\n\nIt's just the back access.\n\nThe trash cans are to the side of the house on the right side when facing the back facade.\n\nI'm looking at a picture from the side of the house from the back alley you can see the terrace and the different floors then moving over to Oh, I forgot to mention the entrance hallway is inspired by the designer that studied architecture in Japan.\n\nSo there's Japanese paper umbrellas on the ceiling which are cleverly put there to filter the light from the spot lights.\n\nso that it's a nice and pleasant lighting as well as provide some nice decoration that is culturally relevant and diverse.\n\nWhich is reflecting the designer's intent to create a space that is inclusive and culturally rich and diverse.\n\nThere is a solid walnut bench with a live edge also and a wabi-sabi inspired little holder that fits ten candles that has been re-imagined as a planter for little cacti.\n\nThere's beautiful natural light throughout and moving to this West Wing studio this is where there is a nice queen bed there's decorations like light sconces that are made from driftwood tree branches that are hanging and have little LED lights lighting up and serving as nightstand lights there's floating nightstand shelves and nice frames and a bedboard with smart bed USB enabled with reclining bed frame and charging ports for cell phone massage function in the smart bed vibrating mattress and a nice teak wood luxury headboard by MASH Studios.\n\nThere's a 55 inch flat-screen TV in every room.\n\nThis room also has a nice tall standing mirror and some antique wooden vases from around the world.\n\nThere's a large bathroom that has a walk-in closet and a large corner shower.\n\nThere's a big sink and bathroom vanity as well as a toilet.\n\nthen onto the other side of the second floor so you go back down the hallway back down the staircase I mean back down to the hallway where the tree is and then back up the other staircase to go to the the rest of the house so the two wings are separated even though they are on the same floor so there's one separate studio that I just described and then there is the rest of the house So coming up on the second floor you enter a nice little hallway with art works by John Fairchild.\n\nThere's a kind of an old Hollywood chic vibe.\n\nThere's art from the Beverly Hills Hotel.\n\nThere's a little bench.\n\nThere's window treatment and flowers and vases and vintage Canada dry wooden drink cases and things of that nature various vintage items as decoration the solid oak hardwood floor throughout the entire house really comes shining through here not literally shining but I mean figuratively speaking there is a nice patina to the freshly refinished floors there's a big laundry setup with a huge capacity washer and dryer all the devices are smart devices the entire home is Google home enabled from the light bulbs to the washer dryer and everything else.\n\nThe first room that you encounter when you get to the second floor on the east wing is a beautiful large double bedroom with big bathroom with double sink.\n\nThese sinks are nice vessel sinks that are resting on a bed of rolled marble rock and a beautiful Carrara marble vanity countertop freshly made vanity in white and then also Carrara marble mosaic flooring the shower is huge in here there is even a bench to sit into the shower and you can easily shower two people in there.\n\nThere's also a toilet in this bathroom and a large walk-in closet like really large walk-in closet.\n\nDecorations here are a beautiful fiddle leaf tree that is 10 foot tall and then a Asian inspired hand carved screen with a mandala cut out of the hand carved wood screen that was made in Thailand.\n\nThe headboard of the bed is also a beautiful teak it's a queen-sized bed all the beds are queen-sized except for the master bed which is king.\n\nThen on the rest of the second floor we have one smaller guest bedroom and then we have one of the most exciting rooms which is the Ebony Oasis also known as as the Wakanda spa.\n\nThe designer has given it this name because it is a inclusive design decision to feature elements that are culturally rich and celebrating African culture, African history, African-American history, and black diaspora by featuring palm pus, dried palm pus flowers around the mirror, kind of like a lion's mane.\n\nThere's a Zulu war shield on the wall in zebra colors, black and white, that is being used as a kind of wabi-sabi interpretation of a light Scott and then there's golden Half spheres That are positioned on the wall as very interesting kind of Make up lights sconces I would say wall lights and then the freestanding vanity bathroom vanity is made from a wooden Nigerian milk bowl with golden faucet so everything in this bathroom is kind of black and gold and then there's a black marble hexagon tile made from Italian black marble with white veining very beautiful the bathtub is also black the toilet is also black and the bathtub is resting on a little bed of black volcanic lava rock which adds a layer of texture to the black bathroom there is also a golden kind of metal lock on the door which looks like a door handle or a thing to knock on the door and it looks like a panther or a line or something so it's kind of like a wig to the black panther.\n\nbasically a cultural celebration of associating black with beautiful bold and luxurious.\n\nMoving on.\n\n[ Background Sounds ] [silence].", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_sp