INFO 03-28 14:03:52 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-2cbe15c178fc4a02a0b6fa90a67b4edc-0: prompt: "CC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 1\nCrime Prevention\n– Instructions &\nTips\nCC100-A Introduction to Criminology\nWeek 9\n1\n© Michelle Dumas 2023\nDue Date\n• Due: Tues, March 28, 2023, by 11:59 pm\n• If you choose to take the 4-day extension for this\nassignment, it must be submitted before Sat, April 1,\n2023, by 11:59 pm.\n• The Dropbox will close on Wed, April 5, 2023, at 11:59\npm.\n• Late penalties will apply to any assignment submitted\nbetween Apr 2 and Apr 5 – 5% per day.\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 2\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 2\nBackground\n• As noted in chapter 11 of the text, Canada, in contrast to\nthe United States, has largely focused on a social\nresponsibility method of crime prevention rather than\nindividual responsibility (Schmalleger & Volk, 2022,\np.282).\n• For this assignment, we will focus on the one that is most\nobservable: protection/avoidance strategies, particularly\nthose achieved through environmental design (also\nknown as CPTED).\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 3\nGoal\n• The goal is to observe and record at 2 different types\nof protection/avoidance strategies in a\nneighbourhood – whether around the University,\nWaterloo, at home, or any other – in Canada.\n• One must be an example of “surveillance” and one\nmust be an example of “access control” (see p. 291 &\n292, chapter 11 and week 10 lecture).\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 4\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 3\nGoal\n• In your report, you will provide photo evidence of\nthese strategies – these photos can only be those\ntaken by you. They should not be from online\nsources or from other students in class.\n• Additionally, written evidence will be provided of the\nCP strategy being used, why they are CP strategies,\nand evaluate them. It is expected to be short and\nsuccinct (maximum 2-page write-up per example).\n[does not include photos – just the write-up sections]\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 5\nStrategy: Surveillance (CPTED)\n• [we will see this next week]\n• Defined\n• Can be “natural” or “mechanical”\n• Assignment: can be natural or mechanical –\nneed to specify\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 6\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 4\nStrategy: Access control (CPTED)\n• Defined\n• Risks of committing crime – becomes harder\n• Assignment: can be natural or mechanical –\nneed to specify\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 7\nAssignment Submissions\n• You can submit more than one assignment if you\nmake changes. Only the most recent file will be\ngraded.\n• You can submit a second file in PDF, as long as\none is in Word/text format\n• It will go through Turnitin.com\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 8\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 5\nBreakdown of Marks (out of 50)\n(15% of final grade)\n• Each Example of CP: 20 marks each (40 total)\n• Photo (5 marks)\n• Strategy type and Crime Prevention (10 marks)\n• Evaluation (5 marks)\n• Formatting (assignment): 5 marks\n• Writing: 5 marks\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 9\nFormatting Entire Assignment (5 marks)\n• Follow instructions (read everything)\n• Submission is an electronic copy in one file in the\nDropbox (MyLS): in Word/text format\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 10\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 6\nFormatting Entire Assignment (cont’d)\n• The paper should be double-spaced, in 12-point Times\nNew Roman font, with one-inch margins in Word\nformat only.\n• It also needs to include a title page that has a title,\nyour name, student ID number, course code and\nname, university name and campus, and instructor’s\nname.\n• Each example needs to start on a new page and use a\ntitle of the strategy type\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 11\nRubric\n(Excellent)\n© Michelle Dumas 2023\n• All formatting instructions\nfollowed, including title\npage requirements, font\nsize, font type, line spacing,\nmargin size, and page\nnumbers. Each example\nhas a subtitle and begins\non a new page. One file is\nsubmitted in MS Word/text\nformat. 12\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 7\nA) Photo & Details (5 marks)\n• A photo and details about where the photo was taken:\nneighbourhood, city, the date it was taken, and time\nof day. This information should be included in the first\nsentence.\n• There should be a general description to your reader.\nThat is, what should I be focused on in the picture(s)?\nThe photo will be graded on the evidence of a crime\nprevention strategy, how clear the strategy is, and its\noriginality (taken by you).\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 13\nA) Photo & Details (cont’d)\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 14\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 8\nRubric\n(Excellent)\n© Michelle Dumas 2023\n• Picture(s) clearly connects to the\ntopic at hand (CP). Demonstrates\nclear understanding of the purpose\nof this assignment. Photo details\nhave been provided (location, date\nand time). A general brief\ndescription is provided to the\nreader. Creativity and originality\nare evident. Photo was taken this\nschool year. [your pics should not\nbe the same as any other student’s\npics] 15\nB) Strategy Type & CP (10 marks)\n• Begin this paragraph by identifying the strategy (i.e.,\nsurveillance or access control).\n• Why is it this type of strategy? Make sure to explain\nyour reasoning by making explicit connections to the\nliterature (textbook and lecture) on these CPTED\nstrategies and to parts of the photo where this is\nexhibited.\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 16\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 9\nB) Strategy Type & CP (cont’d)\n• All relevant factors should be discussed and\nconnected to the details from your picture to provide\nevidence and will be evaluated on this. No online\nsources should be used in this section.\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 17\nB) Strategy Type & CP (cont’d)\n• Additionally, tell the reader how it is preventing crime.\nBe specific and explicit.\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 18\nCC100 3/13/23\n© Michelle Dumas 2023 10\nRubric I\n(Excellent)\n© Michelle Dumas 2023\n• Correctly identifies the type of\nstrategy used (presented in the\nphoto) and whether it is natural or\nmechanical. Explains clearly why\nthis strategy is exemplary. Excellent\nwork in explaining why the strategy\nis applicable by using evidence\nfrom the photo(s) and connecting\nit to the literature on this strategy.\nInformation and evidence are\naccurate, appropriate, and\nintegrated effectively. 19\nRubric II\n(Excellent)\n© Michelle Dumas 2023\n• This fits the criteria of a\nsurveillance or access control\nstrategy.\n• Excellent discussion of the\nways that crime has been\nprevented by this strategy\nwith clear connections to the\nphoto(s). Clear and concise\nexplanations. 20\nA) Photo & Details (cont'd)\n• Picture(s) - should be clear how crime is being prevented; if you need more than one pic, include more than one\n• Mav need more than one - from different angles or close-ups/further back (for context) to back-up arguments\n•Originality: Your pictures should not look like any other students in the class - if vou submit the same thing as another student, you will both receive a zeroPhoto & Details (cont'd)\n•It should have required details:\nneighbourhood/city, time of day & date - this should be in first sentence of first paragraph\n•Description: brief/general - tell me what to look at or what I'm looking at, in case it is not obvious (it is not always obviousB) Strategy Type & CP (cont'd)\n•One way to do this: start with literature (cite in APA) - tell me a descriptor of the strategy and tell me where that is exemplified in the picture; then move to another element & tell me where that is in the picture\n(etc.)Strategy Type & CP (cont'd)\n•Additionally, tell the reader how it is preventing crime.\nBe specific and explicit. (smaller part of this section)\n• That is, how do you believe they are stopping crime from happening?\n• Be specific! Spell it out for me (as if I do not know)\n• You can use lecture & text to back this upEvaluation\n•This is all about your thoughts on it. There is no right or wrong way to answer this - but you need to back up your arguments.\n• Do you think this strategy works in this neighbourhood? [key] Why or why not?\n[consider where it is being used)\n•What improvement could help prevent crime even more? (even if vou think it is successful\n\n请你安装该要求，基于我所提供的两个地点，写一篇英文文章\n\n308 King St N, Waterloo, ON N2J 2Z2\nhttps://www.google.com/maps/place/308+King+St+N,+Waterloo,+ON+N2J+2Z2/@43.4786878,-80.5263162,18z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x882bf3f470e60a2f:0xb0d4560b866ebd82!8m2!3d43.4786859!4d-80.5252219!16s%2Fg%2F11csnl7v20\n该地区是加拿大滑铁卢市的一所在建的豪华公寓，紧邻king street，Regina street和hickory street，其中紧邻Regina street的方向是各种建材和工程车辆进出和施工的地方，这里布满了各个方向的摄像头，大多数都对着这里的出入口和周边的街道，其周围的三条街两边都是居民区，有个人的别墅和大型公寓楼房，也有部分商店，其中大部分是餐馆，车流量很大，周围很热闹。https://www.accommod8u.com/308-king-street-north?gclid=Cj0KCQjw8e-gBhD0ARIsAJiDsaUFiY3gf70Sm1OBJhlGcD01uS\\_gQ0XXr9OmqEoe7hzLxoO84qszC0saAtMjEALw\\_wcB 这是该公寓的网址。\n\nHolbeach Crescent及其周边的街道 https://www.google.com/maps/place/Holbeach+Crescent,+Waterloo,+ON/@43.4900707,-80.5207636,17z/data=!4m15!1m8!3m7!1s0x882bf3948dc70b87:0xa21d7f2c2e446e45!2sHolbeach+Crescent,+Waterloo,+ON!3b1!8m2!3d43.4891289!4d-80.5189719!16s%2Fg%2F1vxw8xms!3m5!1s0x882bf3948dc70b87:0xa21d7f2c2e446e45!8m2!3d43.4891289!4d-80.5189719!16s%2Fg%2F1vxw8xms\n\n该地区是滑铁卢最著名之一的别墅区，其中有许多大型别墅，其中出去早晚高峰之外车流量和居民进出很少。基本上所有别墅都被围墙包围了起来，这些围墙都有2米多高，大部分围墙都经过翻新，用金属材质的栅栏替换了木制栅栏。许多户主在别墅外布置了摄像头，用来监视周围的活动。许多别墅的门口都使用了可视化门铃，一些个人家庭居住的别墅使用了机械结构的钥匙锁，另一些进行出租的别墅则换成了电子的密码锁。该地区挨着滑铁卢的两条主干道，Lexington Rd和Conestoga Pkwy（高速路），车流量极大。该地区还挨着Forwell Trail/Waterloop，是一个公园，时常能看见徒步或是跑步的人。", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=Non