INFO 03-28 14:04:25 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-720ebd64c14841f4b3672f965cdb5ef9-0: prompt: "Job Description:\n\nJob Summary\n\nResponsible for ensuring daily air revenue generation meets or exceeds Company goals while maintaining our low cost brand. Ensure the Revenue Management System has the most accurate inputs and is calibrated accordingly. Recommend and support execution of full-scale strategic changes based on statistical analysis and simulation modeling. Work across multiple customer groups and cross-functional Teams to align Revenue Management strategies with Company initiatives and activities.\nAdditional details and benefits you'll love:\n\nFly for free, as a privilege, on any open seat on all Southwest flights—your eligible dependents too.\nUp to a 9.3% 401(k) Company match, dollar for dollar, per paycheck.\\*\nPotential for annual ProfitSharing contribution toward retirement - when Southwest profits, you profit.\\*\\*\nExplore more Benefits you’ll love: swa.is/benefits\nFor eligible Leadership and individual contributor roles, additional bonus opportunities are available and awarded at the discretion of the company.\nU.S. citizenship or current authorization to work in the U.S. is required, and no current or future work authorization sponsorship available.\nResponsibilities\n\nIncorporate Yield Management and Pricing concepts with Commercial goals to enable Revenue Management to maximize revenue while maintaining our low cost brand\nEnable Yield Management and Pricing to be more effective and efficient by working with more senior members of the Team to create reports and strategies\nIdentify opportunities for revenue generation on Revenue Management, Commercial and Enterprise projects based on analysis with support from Leader\nSeek opportunities within normal scope of work and proactively make recommendations based on system knowledge and analysis to improve revenue performance and meet Revenue Management goals\nRepresent Revenue Management in cross-Team discussions with direct Leadership involvement\nPerform research, mine data, develop conclusions and presenting findings to Leaders for discussion and evaluation\nPresent and communicate occasionally to Revenue Management Senior Leaders\nTrain and mentor junior analysts within the Revenue Management\nMay perform other job duties as directed by Employee’s Leaders\nKnowledge, Skills and Abilities\n\nAdvanced knowledge in Yield Management, Pricing, reservation systems, Global Distribution Systems, forecasting systems and optimization\nAdvanced skills with Microsoft products: Excel (pivot tables, VBA and slicers), Access, Outlook, Teams, etc., advanced skills in SQL and database management and working knowledge of JAVA or Python or Alteryx\nAbility to make sense of, combine, and organize information into meaningful patterns, present this data and provide in meaningful formats so others may continue analysis\nAbility to tell when something is wrong or is likely to go wrong, which may not involve solving the problem, only recognizing there is a problem\nAbility to understand the implications of new information for both current and future problem-solving and decision-making\nAbility to identify and solve complex problems—at times this involves developing unusual or clever ideas but at its core this is using logic and reasoning\nEducation\n\nRequired: High School Diploma or GED\nExperience\n\nAdvanced level experience, seasoned and specialized knowledge in:\nYield Management including theory, strategy and practice (customer demand, bid price controls, dual RBD, etc.)\nPricing including theory, strategy and practice (Fare Basis Codes, ATPCO rules, etc.)\nReservation Systems, Global Distribution Systems\nWorking with large and complex datasets\nHigh level analytical problem solving\nLicensing/Certification\n\nN/A\nPhysical Abilities\n\nAbility to perform work duties from [limited space work station/desk/office area] for extended periods of time\nAbility to communicate and interact with others in the English language to meet the demands of the job\nAbility to use a computer and other office productivity tools with sufficient speed and accuracy to meet the demands of the job\nOther Qualifications\n\nMust maintain a well-groomed appearance per Company appearance standards as described in established guidelines\nMust be a U.S. citizen or have authorization to work in the United States as defined by the Immigration Reform Act of 1986\nMust be at least 18 years of age\nMust be able to comply with Company attendance standards as described in established guidelines Based on the above job description analyze the following resume to check if it passes the ATS screening or not :VIJAY KANASE (H1B Approved)\nEmail: vkanase@okstate.edu LinkedIn-https://www.linkedin.com/in/vijay-kanase/ Phone: 405-780-5053\nEDUCATION:\n\nMaster of Science in Industrial Engineering and Management August 2019 - May 2021\n Oklahoma State University – Stillwater, OK GPA 3.7/4.0\n• Supply Chain Strategy • Integrated Manufacturing & Planning • Data Analytics & Visualization\n\nBachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering July 2013 – July 2017\nUniversity of Pune, India GPA 3.6/4.0\n• Manufacturing Processes • Industrial Engineering • Operation Research\n\nSKILLS:\n• Data Analytics: MySQL, Advanced Excel, SQL, Tableau\n• Statistical Analysis: Regression, Predictive Modeling\n• Supply Chain: Forecasting, Logistics, Network Optimization • Problem-Solving: Root Cause Analysis, Value Stream Mapping\n• Communication: Business Process Mapping & Periodic Business Presentations\n• Technical: SAP, Zoho Projects, Microsoft Office Suite\n\nSUPPLY CHAIN EXPERIENCE:\n \nSupply Chain Analyst – Salad and Go, AZ, USA Mar 2022 – Present \n• Created labour and transportation forecasting models for financial & operational planning, reducing costs and driving efficiency.\n• Responsible for supporting ad hoc modelling and developing tools for production, P&L, logistics, and distribution activities.\n• Gathered, manipulated, cleaned, and analysed structured and unstructured data sources helping leaders in supply chain to \n• reduce costs and drive efficiency.\n• Developed open action tool using Tableau and Azure data studio to monitor & collect data on current operations across supply\nchain including operations, warehousing, storage, and delivery.\n• Used 3TO for supply chain network modelling to choose a facility in West coast & Southeast region of US worth $60M.\n• Used SQL to write queries & create database which acted as a backend for network optimization software – 3TO\n\nSupply Chain Analyst – Customer Success – - Supply Chain Wizard, NJ, USA July 2021 – December 2021 \n• Continuously monitor multiple client statuses to ensure issue-free usage of the products like OEE Tracker, Digital Logbook.\n• Perform OEE analysis to measure availability, quality, and performance to administer the opportunity for improvement.\n• Provided suggestions to client via business process mapping using data analysis via Excel and visualizations via Tableau.\n• Resolved complex business problems using creative problem solving & organized periodic business presentations for clients.\n• Managed both functional and non-functional business requirements as well as new requested requirements using JIRA\n\nProcess Engineer – Wilo Mather & Platt, Pune, India Oct 2017 – April 2018\n• Conduct Root cause analysis and implement corrective actions to address quality issues and prevent recurrence.\n• Achieved 20% productivity increase by creating Value Stream Map for pump assembly line to eliminate NVA.\n\nGraduate Trainee – Vishwaraj Industries, Pune, India May 2018 – April 2019\n• Analyzed supplier performance data to identify areas for improvement and develop corrective actions.\n• Provided training and guidance to suppliers on quality requirements, standards, and procedures.\n\nManufacturing an ATV, SAE BAJA, University of Pune, India Project Duration: Jul 2013 – May 2017\n• Lead and managed a team of 25 individuals securing 9 national awards & stood 6th overall in world for SAE BAJA International.\n• Responsible for supply chain management at sub assembly level, finalize quotations and supplier negotiations for material procurement, manufacturing of all subsystems system, and material testing.\n\nADDITIONAL PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\nGraduate Research Assistant – Oklahoma State University – Stillwater, OK August 2021 – July 2021 \n• Analysed experiment data and equipment specifications to establish standard operating procedures for individual experiments\n\nCAMPUS PROJECTS AND ACTIVITIES:\n\nTransportation Modelling Network optimization in Supply Chain Guru \n• Tasked to develop a transportation network optimization model in Llamasoft Supply Chain Guru to redesign the DC network.\n• Created a dashboard and visualized the comparison of scenarios to maximize percent of demand served with 97% service level\n\nImplementing Relational Database Management System Using MySQL and MS Access \n• Implemented a RDBMS (M-Trak) in Microsoft-access and MySQL to record, edit & generate reports using MySQL queries. \n\nHead of Sports (Badminton) - Oklahoma State University – Elected President August 2020 – May 2021\n• Managed and organized all facets of sport events including budgeting, logistics, team building & execution.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [12245, 7662, 1447, 12245, 21517, 271, 1061, 42319, 369, 22573, 7298, 3720, 12957, 9471, 20027, 476, 35275, 8188, 8845, 1393, 20337, 1039, 3347, 2783, 6741, 13, 2927