INFO 03-28 14:04:29 [logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-ea79c9ba2129422c8e076f98b2a7998d-0: prompt: '\\*\\*contents\\*\\*:\nThe 2022 regular National Assembly is noisy due to the revision of the Grain Control Act. In the newspaper, there is also a cynical expression of the "Rice Mandatory Purchase Act" and the "Rice Market Quarantine Act." The bill, being pushed by the opposition Democratic Party of Korea, calls for the government to spend its budget to keep rice prices mandatory at some point. If rice production is more than 3% higher than expected demand in Korea or if rice prices fall more than 5% from the previous year, the government is obligated to buy excess supplies and "market quarantine" (some resell while storing them after purchase). The main logic of the opposition is whether they can afford to maintain higher rice prices at a huge cost than international prices, and that it is not right to provide such support only to rice when food self-sufficiency rates such as other grains and meat continue to fall. The government\'s mandatory purchase of rice, which caused controversy over populism due to the cost of more than 1 trillion won a year, is reasonable.\n[Agreed] Considering the specificity of grains and rice, which are difficult to control production depending on market conditions, the difficulty of production farmers has increased due to the fall in domestic rice prices. Rice prices have been on the decline while all prices are on a high march due to worsening inflation, which makes farmers feel more frustrated. Compared to last year\'s harvest season, the price dropped by about 30%. As 2021 inventories are piled up all over the country, the price decline could worsen when the rice harvest season enters. Considering the cost of fertilizer and labor costs that went into production, farmers suffered a significant deficit. Even farmers who turn over rice produced with sweat into tractors have appeared. The government should take measures against farmers.\n\nUntil now, there have been market quarantine measures by the government. However, the only amendment to the law is to change the method of purchasing the lowest price on the side of farmers to the extent that the government automatically intervenes and quarantines if production exceeds the mandatory provision. Although the function of the market is important, agricultural products, especially rice, which is a traditional staple, have their own characteristics that cannot be solved by market logic. In the past, the government has decided to introduce foreign rice to foster other industries in the process of opening up trade, so there is a reason to continue to compensate farmers. Last year, the excess domestic production was 270,000 tons, but the government has to import 400,000 tons, so it is also responsible for that.\n\nRice is an important grain that is difficult to increase or reduce production easily depending on market conditions. Rice paddies are also decreasing in a situation where cultivated land is generally decreasing. The controversy over short-term overproduction is also meaningless because once the production green space is reduced, it is impossible to recover. In the end, the government should play a role in buying if production is overflowing, and releasing savings if it is insufficient. There is no choice but to execute the required budget for market isolation of such functions. For this reason, it is also worth noting that provincial governors from eight regions across the country, the main producer of rice, visited the National Assembly and issued a statement calling for "calling for measures to stabilize rice prices." Rice should be recognized for its specificity. It is difficult to leave it unattended any longer.[Conversely] Storage costs are as high as purchase costs...Resolution of restructuring such as converting to a "strategic crop" In 2021, the budget for quarantining 370,000 tons of excess production in the market alone was 848.9 billion won. With 500,000 tons expected to be overproduced this year, a purchase budget of more than 1 trillion won is needed. The purchase cost alone is about this much. It rather costs a lot more to keep. Not all stockpiles are digested in one year. Due to the surplus of rice every year, it is impossible to recover funds by selling the rice purchased. Should such expenses be spent at the pan-government level when the government calls for austerity and reorganizes dry towels to reduce spending budgets? The economy is very difficult due to already severe inflation, and this recession may end at any time.\n\nThe logic of placing a special status on rice alone is also absurd. Rice consumption continues to decline, especially among the younger generation, and flour products and meat consumption are increasing rapidly. Soybeans and other grains are mostly dependent on imports. If rice production far exceeds consumption and the self-sufficiency rate of food falls, the answer is set. Rice production should be reduced and other crops and meat production should be increased. As the government purchases rice at unreasonable prices that are far from the market price every year, farmers believe in this purchase system and fall into a vicious cycle of overproduction. If the government is responsible for both rice and transportation costs, where does the government come from?\n\nThe government should not encourage overproduction with "forced government purchases" and worsen the reality of agriculture, but change its thinking. The public law is to restructure agriculture by expanding smart farms, expanding strategic crops, and allowing and inducing companies to enter agriculture. It is difficult to be a food countermeasure in the era of the 4th Industrial Revolution by producing only rice that has been far from stocks for a long time because it is easy to farm. Moreover, food imports are increasing, and costs are increasing exponentially. It is urgent to establish realistic food measures. It is necessary to induce other economical crops to be grown in rice paddies right away. The cost of agricultural aid should be spent on this.생각 Thinking - Rice remains due to a sharp drop in consumption, but 99.5% wheat and 63.2% soybeans are imported... It is true that farmers\' worries deepened as the price of a bag of 80kg rice, which exceeded 220,000 won in 2021, fell to 167,000 won in a year. The per capita consumption, which reached 116.3kg in 1991, fell to 69.8kg in 2012 and 56.9kg in 2021, but the supply remained the same, which is a natural result. This is largely due to the government\'s failure to actively use policies to induce rice farmers to turn their attention to other strategic crops, rather than a temporary measure of government purchases. Another problem is that even if the government starts to quarantine the market, the demand for farmers\' purchases will increase. Until when can the government buy excess production or increase consumption sharply? The government should move away from short-term measures and improve the constitution of Korean agriculture. The answer is if the self-sufficiency rate of food is only 20 percent, with 99.5 percent of wheat and 63.2 percent of soybeans imported while rice remains. Rather than unconditionally protecting cultivated land, it is necessary to make farmland more efficient, and to pave the way for companies to enter so that agriculture becomes a high-tech industry.\n\n\\*\\*system\\*\\*: You must follow the steps in \'{steps}\' to answer \'{questions}\'.\nFocus on the content of \'{contents}\' when configuring responses.\n\n\\*\\*steps\\*\\*:\n‘Observation == false’\n!IMPORTANT : Repeat until the final answer is obtained.\n\nrespond with a JSON in the format:\n\n```json\n{\nIf ‘Observation = false’, then:\n“Thought” : string // Consider what is necessary to answer the question.\n“Action”: string // Write an article focusing on \'{contents}\' to address \'{question}\'.\n“Observation” : boolean // true or false. Observe the results of the action. If the answer is sufficient, set ‘Observation = true’. If the answer is insufficient, set ‘Observation = false’.\n\nElse if ‘Observation = true’, then:\nFinal Answer: string // Provide the final answer to the original input question.\n}\n\'\'\'\n\n\\*\\*question\\*\\*:\n- - Please set the topic of grain management.\n- - Please pick 10 topics.\n- - Detailed and clear issues are needed to be raised.\nAnswer in English.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.1, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [59, 46127, 9, 17610, 59, 46127, 9, 510, 785, 220, 17, 15, 17, 17, 5792, 5055, 11738, 374, 49280, 4152, 311, 279, 23578, 315, 279, 74274, 7779, 3218, 13, 758, 279, 16803, 11, 1052, 374, 1083, 264, 69679, 7493, 315, 279, 330, 49, 558, 70782, 30988, 3218, 1, 323, 279, 330, 49, 558, 7993, 92745, 38357, 3218, 1189, 576, 4031, 11, 1660, 15391, 553, 279, 13758, 11396, 8554, 315, 11862, 11, 6738, 369, 279, 3033, 311, 8329, 1181, 8039, 311, 2506, 19653, 7576, 23042, 518, 1045, 1459, 13, 1416, 19653, 5670, 374, 803, 1091, 220, 18, 4, 5080, 1091, 3601, 7479, 304, 11862, 476, 421, 19653, 7576, 4399, 803, 1091, 220, 20, 4, 504, 279, 3681, 1042, 11, 279, 3033, 374, 66876, 311, 3695, 13623, 16720, 323, 330, 19301, 70389, 1, 320, 14689, 592, 613, 1393, 27572, 1105, 1283, 7627, 568, 576, 1887, 12218, 315, 279, 13758, 374, 3425, 807, 646, 9946, 311, 10306, 5080, 19653, 7576, 518, 264, 6765, 2783, 1091, 6489, 7576, 11, 323, 429, 432, 374, 537, 1290, 311, 3410, 1741, 1824, 1172, 311, 19653, 979, 3607, 656, 1331, 1362, 10387, 7813, 1741, 438, 1008, 40836, 323, 13041